  Questions:
  - QuestionText: Argon is in the liquid state between which temperature range?
    Options:
    - "-200\xB0C to -185.8\xB0C"
    - " -189.3\xB0C to -185.8\xB0C"
    - " -189.3\xB0C to -190\xB0C"
    - "-195\xB0C to -185.8\xB0C"
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    IsTrueFalse: 0
    CorrectAnswer: 0
    CorrectFeedback: "\_Excellent! Argon remains in the liquid state between -189.3\xB0C
      and -185.8\xB0C."
    IncorrectFeedback: "Not quite! The correct answer is  -183\xB0C. At this temperature,
      oxygen  changes from gas to liquid. Try again!"
  - QuestionText: "At temperatures below -189.3\xB0C, Argon exists as a solid."
    Options:
    - True
    - False
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    IsTrueFalse: 0
    CorrectAnswer: 0
    CorrectFeedback: "Perfect! Argon freezes below -189.3\xB0C and stays solid."
    IncorrectFeedback: "Not correct. Below -189.3\xB0C, Argon becomes a solid. "
